Hardware Pinout Report

-As of today, October 29th, the hardware team implemented an ESP32 that in conjunction with a 12V Power Supply and a buck booster converter, controls the power to the
fan and PTC heating element. The hardware team has also implemented switching capabilities for both the PTC element and the fan via a relay through the esp32 and a 
mosfet through an arduino uno r4. 

ESP32 Pinout
D13 - Common ground between the ESP32 and the Arduino to enable MOSFET switching
GND - Common ground between the buck boost converter and the power supply (negative end)

ARDUINO R4 Pinout
9 - Logic Pin connected to the gate of the MOSFET, turns MOSFET on/off for switching function
5V - Powers the fan
GND - Hooked up to GND on the ESP32 to provide a common ground (essential for MOSFET function)
